hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"198","Jazāka Allāhu khayran. May Allah reward you with goodness."
"199","Man ḥafaʿa ʿashra āyāt min awwali sūratil-kahfi ʿuṣima minad-dajjāl, wal-istiʿādhahi billahi min fitnatihi ʿaqibat-tashahhudi al-akhīri min kulli ṣalāh.. Whoever memorizes ten verses from the beginning of Surah Al-Kahf will be protected from the Dajjal (the Antichrist), and seeking refuge in Allah from his tribulation after the last Tashahhud of every prayer."
